WebP plug-in for Lumen 1.0
==========================

Lets Lumen import, show, adjust and export WebP pictures (.webp): what
web pages, many phones and editors, and Google's tools save. Lossy and
lossless WebP both work, with or without transparency (laid on white).
For an animated WebP, Lumen shows its first frame.

It is a small program, LumenWebP, which Lumen runs in the background for
each WebP picture it needs: for a thumbnail and for the Viewer it decodes
the picture straight to the size wanted, which is quick. Decoding uses
NEON when the processor has it.

It lives in Lumen's Plugins directory (!Lumen.Plugins.WebP). PackMan
puts it there. Or drag the WebP directory from the zip into Lumen's
Plug-ins > Add plug-in window (it works at once), or it is found the
next time Lumen starts. It is a format plug-in: its Plugin file tells
Lumen which files are WebP pictures, so it needs Lumen 0.0.38 or later.
They are imported once it is there.

A WebP picture's EXIF (the camera, the date and where it was taken) is
read too, so WebP pictures with a position can be shown on a map.

Memory: LumenWebP needs memory only while it works: about 40 MB to
decode a 12 megapixel lossy picture at full size, and about 90 MB for a
lossless one. Thumbnails need much less.

The LumenWebP User Guide is in Guide (Guide.index/html): open it in your
web browser.

libwebp is copyright (C) Google Inc. and used under its BSD licence;
the licence, and Google's patent grant for WebP, are in Licence.
LumenWebP itself is copyright (C) 2026 Andrew Youll and released under
the MIT licence. Its source is in Lumen's source (plugins.webp, with
deps.build-webp.sh, which builds libwebp for it).
